# Code Flow Comments

Every non-trivial code path should be understandable step-by-step. **5-second test:** a teammate reads one step for ~5 seconds. If they still don't know why it runs or what it produces, fix that step.

## Two layers

1. **Section blocks** — divide multi-step logic into named phases
2. **Inline step comments** — one short `//` above each logical step inside a section

Skip both on trivial one-liners. Prefer clear names over comments that restate the code.

## Section blocks

Use when a function has **2+ distinct phases** and the phase is **≥ 10 lines**. Under 10 lines: inline `//` only.

```typescript
/* ----------------------------- Load blueprint ----------------------------- */
/* --------------------------- Apply ME / TE ------------------------------- */
/* ----------------------------- Schedule jobs ------------------------------ */
```

Centered dash style, same total width (~78 chars) within a file.

## Inline step comments

One line; state what the step does or why when non-obvious.

```typescript
async function schedulePlanRoots(roots: PlanRootEntry[]) {
  /* ----------------------------- Load blueprint ----------------------------- */

  // Resolve BPO recipe from SDE — throws if type id missing from static data
  const bp = getBlueprint(root.blueprintTypeId)
  if (!bp) throw new Error('Blueprint not found')

  // Job duration uses TE + Industry skills per eve-industry-domain.mdc
  const seconds = jobDurationSeconds(bp, root.me, root.te, skills, runs)

  /* ----------------------------- Schedule jobs ------------------------------ */

  // Sub-components must finish before parent manufacturing slot opens
  await scheduleDependencies(root, bp.materials)

  // Assign earliest free slot respecting mass production limits
  assignSlot(root.id, seconds)
}
```

| Step comment should… | Step comment should not… |
|---|---|
| Name the step's purpose | Repeat the next line verbatim |
| Explain hidden game rules | Describe obvious guards |
| Note ordering or side effects | Replace bad names |

## JSDoc

On **exported** functions/types whose purpose is not obvious from the name. Skip tests, trivial one-liners, and React components (use section comments instead).

Document game-mechanics helpers with assumptions (ME rounding, batch runs, hub prices).

## Anti-patterns

- Section banner over < 10 lines
- Uneven banner widths in the same file
- Step comments instead of renames
- Long orchestrators with neither sections nor step comments
